Description: Disable assert macro redefinition for abseil compatibility
 Chromium's base/logging.h redefines assert to DLOG_ASSERT at line 591-592.
 This breaks abseil's str_format constexpr code (constexpr_parser.h, bind.h,
 arg.h, extension.h) which requires the standard assert macro from <cassert>
 for compile-time format checking.
 .
 When is_official_build=true, abseil's compile-time format checking is enabled,
 and any code path that includes base/logging.h before abseil str_format headers
 will fail with "use of undeclared identifier 'assert'" errors.
 .
 Fix by commenting out the assert redefinition. This is a cleaner fix than
 patching individual abseil headers.
Author: Juan Manuel Mendez Rey <vejeta@gmail.com>
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/915400
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2025-12-05

diff --git a/base/logging.h b/base/logging.h
index 13ebd3b..46ed019 100644
--- a/base/logging.h
+++ b/base/logging.h
@@ -587,9 +587,11 @@ BASE_EXPORT extern LogSeverity LOGGING_DCHECK;
 constexpr LogSeverity LOGGING_DCHECK = LOGGING_FATAL;
 #endif  // BUILDFLAG(DCHECK_IS_CONFIGURABLE)

-// Redefine the standard assert to use our nice log files
-#undef assert
-#define assert(x) DLOG_ASSERT(x)
+// Chromium originally redefined assert to DLOG_ASSERT, but this breaks
+// abseil's str_format constexpr code which requires the standard assert
+// macro from <cassert>. Disable the redefinition.
+// #undef assert
+// #define assert(x) DLOG_ASSERT(x)

 // This class more or less represents a particular log message.  You
 // create an instance of LogMessage and then stream stuff to it.
